First, convert all travel times to minutes. The walk takes 10 minutes. The train ride is 1 hour 20 minutes, which equals $60 + 20 = 80$ minutes. The total travel time is $10 + 80 = 90$ minutes.

Counting back 90 minutes from the arrival deadline of 0900 hours: subtracting 60 minutes brings us to 0800 hours. Subtracting the remaining 30 minutes gives 0730 hours. Therefore, Pete must leave by 0730 hours to arrive on time.

