First, determine each runner's time for their 200-meter leg. Rhonda's time is given as 18 seconds. Sally takes 2 seconds longer than Rhonda, so her time is 18 + 2 = 20 seconds. Diane runs 3 seconds faster than Rhonda, so her time is 18 - 3 = 15 seconds.

To find the total race time, sum the individual times: 18 + 20 + 15. Adding these together gives 38 + 15 = 53 seconds. The total time for the 600-meter relay is the sum of the parts.

