First, determine the highest score already achieved. One student scored 95%. The other missed 3 out of 40 questions, meaning they got $40 - 3 = 37$ right. Their percentage is $37 \div 40 = 0.925$, or 92.5%. The current top score is 95%. To have the strictly highest score, Hannah must beat 95%.

Calculate 95% of 40 questions: $0.95 \times 40 = 38$. Hannah needs more than 38 correct answers. Since there are only 40 questions total, the next possible integer is 39. Getting 39 right is $39 \div 40 = 97.5\%$, which beats 95%.

