First, calculate the number of fuel tanks needed. The trip is 2000 miles, and one tank lasts 500 miles, so she needs $2000 \div 500 = 4$ tanks. Let $x$ be the cost to fill one tank. The total fuel cost is $4x$.

The problem states the food cost is $3/5$ times the total fuel cost, so food cost is $\frac{3}{5}(4x) = 2.4x$. The total spending is the sum of fuel and food costs: $4x + 2.4x = 6.4x$. We know the total is $288, so we set up the equation $6.4x = 288$.

Solving for $x$: $x = 288 \div 6.4 = 45$. The cost to fill one tank is $45. \boxed{45}

